      "message": "Since the ARMv7-M (PMSAv7) and ARMv8-M (PMSAv8) MPU implementations share almost no code ([Differences between Armv7-M and Armv8-M MPU](https://developer.arm.com/documentation/107565/0101/Introduction/Differences-between-Armv7-M-and-Armv8-M-MPU) — only `mpu_static_rollback_region_id`, the `SYS_INIT` registration, and the `\u003c 0` check are shared), could we split this into two files (`mpu_v7m.c` and `mpu_v8m.c`) selected in `zephyr/shim/core/cortex-m/CMakeLists.txt` instead of adding nested `#ifdef CONFIG_CPU_CORTEX_M33` blocks?\n\nSpecifically:\n\n1. **`git mv zephyr/shim/core/cortex-m/mpu.c zephyr/shim/core/cortex-m/mpu_v7m.c`** (keeping the existing ARMv7-M implementation untouched).\n\n2. **Select the source file in `zephyr/shim/core/cortex-m/CMakeLists.txt`** using the ARMv8-M Kconfig symbols (matching how upstream Zephyr\u0027s `arch/arm/core/mpu/arm_mpu.c` checks for ARMv8-M before ARMv7-M, since Cortex-M33 also selects `CONFIG_ARMV7_M_ARMV8_M_MAINLINE`):\n```cmake\nif (CONFIG_MPU)\n  if (CONFIG_ARMV8_M_BASELINE OR CONFIG_ARMV8_M_MAINLINE)\n    zephyr_library_sources(mpu_v8m.c)\n  else()\n    zephyr_library_sources(mpu_v7m.c)\n  endif()\nendif()\n```\n\n3. **Add `zephyr/shim/core/cortex-m/mpu_v8m.c`** without the architecture `#ifdef`s. While doing so, please also address two issues in the ARMv8-M rollback logic:\n   * **Lock rollback at boot**: `arm_cmse_mpu_region_get()` uses the `TT` (Test Target) instruction, which only reports a valid `MREGION` (`MRVALID \u003d\u003d 1`) when the target address matches an **enabled** MPU region (see [TT, TTT, TTA, and TTAT](https://developer.arm.com/documentation/100235/0100/The-Cortex-M33-Instruction-Set/Miscellaneous-instructions/TT--TTT--TTA--and-TTAT) in the Cortex-M33 Generic User Guide, and [DDI 0553](https://developer.arm.com/documentation/ddi0553/bz/) Section D1.2.269 `TT_RESP`). Because `mpu_regions.c` defines `\"ROLLBACK\"` with `REGION_FLASH_ATTR` and `z_arm_mpu_init()` enables it ([`MPU_RLAR.EN \u003d 1`](https://developer.arm.com/documentation/100235/0100/The-Cortex-M33-Peripherals/Security-Attribution-and--Memory-Protection/MPU-Region-Limit-Address-Register)) at boot, `mpu_add_static_rollback_regions()` needs to call `mpu_lock_rollback(true)` right after looking up the region index so the rollback region starts locked at `PRE_KERNEL_1` (matching ARMv7-M behavior).\n   * **Memory barriers (`DSB` + `ISB`)**: Per [Updating protected memory regions](https://developer.arm.com/documentation/100235/0100/The-Cortex-M33-Peripherals/Security-Attribution-and--Memory-Protection/Updating-protected-memory-regions) and [Configuring an MPU region](https://developer.arm.com/documentation/107565/0100/Memory-protection/MPU-programmers-model/Configuring-an-MPU-region) (as well as [DDI 0553](https://developer.arm.com/documentation/ddi0553/bz/) Section B8.3 *The System Control Space (SCS)*, rules `RBMLS`/`RWQQB`), updates to SCS MPU registers require a `DSB` followed by an `ISB` (`barrier_dsync_fence_full()` and `barrier_isync_fence_full()`) to guarantee the new MPU state is visible before subsequent memory accesses (such as the immediate `memcpy` in `read_rollback()`).\n   * **Comments on `P_NA` and `PRIVDEFENA`**: Reference [`MPU_RBAR.AP[2:1]`](https://developer.arm.com/documentation/100235/0100/The-Cortex-M33-Peripherals/Security-Attribution-and--Memory-Protection/MPU-Region-Base-Address-Register) (which has no \"Privileged No-Access\" encoding) and [`MPU_CTRL.PRIVDEFENA`](https://developer.arm.com/documentation/100235/0100/The-Cortex-M33-Peripherals/Security-Attribution-and--Memory-Protection/Memory-Protection-Unit).\n\nFor example, `zephyr/shim/core/cortex-m/mpu_v8m.c` would look like:\n```c\n/* Copyright 2026 The ChromiumOS Authors\n * Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be\n * found in the LICENSE file.\n */\n\n#include \"common.h\"\n#include \"config.h\"\n#include \"mpu.h\"\n\n#include \u003cerrno.h\u003e\n#include \u003cstdbool.h\u003e\n\n#include \u003czephyr/arch/cpu.h\u003e\n#include \u003czephyr/devicetree.h\u003e\n#include \u003czephyr/init.h\u003e\n#include \u003czephyr/kernel.h\u003e\n#include \u003czephyr/logging/log.h\u003e\n#include \u003czephyr/sys/barrier.h\u003e\n\n#include \u003ccmsis_core.h\u003e\n#include \u003ccortex_m/cmse.h\u003e\n\nLOG_MODULE_REGISTER(shim_mpu, LOG_LEVEL_ERR);\n\nvoid mpu_enable(void)\n{\n\t/* MPU is configured and enabled by Zephyr init code. */\n}\n\n#ifdef CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_ROLLBACK_MPU_PROTECT\nstatic int mpu_static_rollback_region_id \u003d -1;\n\ntest_mockable int mpu_lock_rollback(bool lock)\n{\n\tif (mpu_static_rollback_region_id \u003c 0) {\n\t\treturn -EINVAL;\n\t}\n\n\t/*\n\t * On ARMv8-M, MPU_RBAR.AP[2:1] does not have a \"Privileged No-Access\"\n\t * encoding (DDI 0553 Sec D1.2.171). Disabling the MPU region here\n\t * relies on the privileged default memory map being disabled\n\t * (MPU_CTRL.PRIVDEFENA \u003d\u003d 0 via CONFIG_MPU_DISABLE_BACKGROUND_MAP\u003dy,\n\t * DDI 0553 Sec D1.2.168) to generate a MemManage fault on access.\n\t */\n\tMPU-\u003eRNR \u003d mpu_static_rollback_region_id;\n\tif (lock) {\n\t\tMPU-\u003eRLAR \u0026\u003d ~MPU_RLAR_EN_Msk;\n\t} else {\n\t\tMPU-\u003eRLAR |\u003d MPU_RLAR_EN_Msk;\n\t}\n\n\tbarrier_dsync_fence_full();\n\tbarrier_isync_fence_full();\n\n\treturn 0;\n}\n\nstatic int mpu_add_static_rollback_regions(void)\n{\n\t/*\n\t * On ARMv8-M, overlapping enabled MPU regions fault (DDI 0553 Sec\n\t * B10.1, rule RLLLP), so the rollback region is defined as a separate\n\t * static entry in mpu_regions[] (e.g., shim/chip/rtkfp/mpu_regions.c)\n\t * and enabled during z_arm_mpu_init(). Look up its region index while\n\t * enabled (required for TT_RESP.MRVALID, DDI 0553 Sec D1.2.269) and\n\t * then immediately lock (disable) it.\n\t */\n\tint region \u003d arm_cmse_mpu_region_get(\n\t\tCONFIG_MAPPED_STORAGE_BASE +\n\t\tDT_REG_ADDR(DT_NODELABEL(rollback0)));\n\n\tif (region \u003c 0) {\n\t\treturn -EINVAL;\n\t}\n\n\tmpu_static_rollback_region_id \u003d region;\n\tLOG_DBG(\"Rollback MPU region set at %d\", region);\n\n\treturn mpu_lock_rollback(true);\n}\nSYS_INIT(mpu_add_static_rollback_regions, PRE_KERNEL_1, 50);\n#endif /* CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_ROLLBACK_MPU_PROTECT */\n```",
